cff-version: 1.2.0
title: INQETRA — research-design studio and UK built-environment dataset hub
message: >-
  If you use INQETRA in your research, please cite it using this metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Mohamed Hamdy Ali
    email: M.HamdyMohamedAli3267@student.leedsbeckett.ac.uk
    affiliation: Leeds Beckett University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6074-8524"
version: 0.2.2
date-released: "2026-09-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohamedHamdy-1991/INQETRA"
url: "https://inqetra.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  INQETRA is a web-based research-design studio and dataset hub for the UK built
  environment. It links research problems, questions, aims, methods and dataset
  requirements to a curated catalogue of 751 authoritative datasets, performs
  rule-based compatibility and gap analysis, and exports reproducible, provenance-
  traceable Research Data Plans. An optional provider-neutral AI assistant is
  restricted to structuring deterministic tool outputs.
keywords:
  - research design
  - open data
  - built environment
  - data management plan
  - provenance
  - energy
  - housing
  - climate
